module gunbc.plans.cardinality_refinement

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn cardinality_refinement_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Goal: one cardinality axis for emptiness, length and bounded magnitude, propagated through folds. This is the 2026-07-31 scoping proposal, not current implementation standing. DESIGN and domain carriers govern implementation; the historical where/refine proposal below requires reconciliation with the current checked-constructor model before authoring parser/checker changes."),
    p(text: "Boundary: arbitrary Validation.admits predicates remain runtime constructor checks. Only a closed, decidable cardinality fragment may enter static checking/fold propagation: Length<N>, NonEmpty, Bounded<Lo,Hi>, Width<N>, expressed over counts/magnitude. A bound beyond machine width is typed Rejected, never wrapping; no arbitrary predicate may leak into static inference."),
    p(text: "Existing observations: v2.std.refinement Validation/Refined/refine already returns Accepted/Rejected, with integer factories and ordering refinements. Refined still exposed base without consuming sole_constructor; generic/every-construction/compiler-exemption coverage of type_has_sole_constructor / SoleConstructorViolation was unverified. MachineWidth had a phantom parameter without value reflection; std.bit.Byte had an unchecked List<Bit>. Re-read these owners rather than assuming those gaps persist."),
    p(text: "Historical obligations: P1 alias/field cardinality surface through dag_grammar_type_alias_rhs_expr, record grammar, v2.std.compilers.sugar and normalize_sugar_key_optional into Validation plus a construction obligation. P2 positive/negative probes of generic Refined and every construction form/exemption; then consume the existing sanctioned factory wall, extending only measured escapes. Unauthorized construction must produce located SoleConstructorViolation, never a parallel checker."),
    p(text: "P3 closed cardinality vocabulary only; proposed Byte Length<8> and bounded Int64 derive from that authority. P4 fold_node/catamorphism computes list length and combined bounds, borrowing the cost-through-fold algebra’s shape; overflow refuses and a miscounting fold must red. P5 stretch: reflect type-level Nat into value width so bits_per_byte and bounds derive from types."),
    p(text: "Historical pipeline: modeled tokenize/parse→sugar normalize→construction discharge/cardinality propagation→erase refinement or target assert. Parser/normalizer edits are load-bearing and follow lock-down. First execution: eight-bit Byte accepted, seven-bit rejected; then one List<Bit> length fold replaces consumer checks; then NonEmpty/Bounded and add-overflow; finally type-level reflection/static cases. These controls, not surface syntax alone, validate the feature. The intended consumers include Byte, bounded integers, typed coercion and nonempty strings/diagnostics."),
  ]
}

data cardinality_refinement_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "cardinality-refinement",
  title: "Plan — Cardinality refinement (the decidable fold-propagated refinement axis)",
  body: cardinality_refinement_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when `Byte = \{ bits: List<Bit> \} where Length<8>` is authored, its construction is compiler-enforced, and a 7-bit byte is a typed `Rejected` green-by-execution — at which point `bit.dag`'s \"length not checked\", `bits_per_byte`'s centralized `8`, and the `MachineWidth` phantom gap all dissolve into the carriers, and this scoping is redundant.")
  }
}
